# Changelog

All notable changes to this project are tracked here. This changelog follows
[Keep a Changelog](https://keepachangelog.com/en/1.1.0/) and
[Semantic Versioning](https://semver.org/).

## How to use this file

- Keep `## [Unreleased]` at the top and add bullets as changes land.
- Invoke `$publish-release --tag X.Y.Z` from this project to prepare, commit,
  push and merge the release PR, tag the verified merged commit in
  `__MAIN_BRANCH__` history, and verify published assets.
- If GitHub requires approval, follow the displayed link. The skill waits up
  to ten minutes and continues automatically when an eligible reviewer approves.
- After a timeout or interruption, use `$publish-release --resume --tag X.Y.Z`.
- The generated shell helper exposes private content/tag/push/verify primitives;
  it does not commit or publish branches. The skill delegates those effects to
  the existing canonical commit/PR owner.
- Preparation refuses conflicting tags and preserves separation between sections.
  Runtime version verification follows local annotated-tag creation and precedes
  remote push, so SCM-derived versions resolve correctly.
- Release section format:
  `## [__PROJECT_TAG_PREFIX__-vX.Y.Z] - YYYY-MM-DD`

